Start with product discovery. Make strong recommendations and minimize questions, but stop for decisions that materially affect the business model, permissions, money, sensitive data, irreversible architecture, or production release.

For architecture, inspect the existing codebase and research current primary sources. Compare at least three realistic options, explain trade-offs and failure modes, and record the decision in `.auto-company/architecture/ADR-0001.md`.

For UX, define the user journey, information architecture, screen/state matrix, accessibility, and one coherent design direction before implementation.

Implement only an approved, traceable production slice. Run objective checks and update `.auto-company/evidence/release-evidence.md`. Never merge or deploy to production without explicit approval.

